                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "225476338",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561197991482494",
                            "num_reviews": 88,
                            "playtime_forever": 133,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 133,
                            "last_played": 1778769386
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I expect an adventure game of this vintage to be weird and confusing, which is why I was willing to bang my head against it for a couple hours before going online and seeing what others had to say. While there's some truth to my initial assumption, it appears the Steam version of [i]Atlantis II[/i] is uniquely bungled and not worth another second of my time or yours.\n\nWhich is a pity. Sorta. This game is the kind of quirky relic that speaks to me. It's also heavy on cumbersome mazes and depictions of real-world cultures that... Well, look, I haven't done thorough research, and I don't have the personal background to tell you how accurate or respectful any of this is, but based on what information I [i]can[/i] find about the developers, I'm not alone in that. Maybe we just let this one stay in the past.",
